<p></p>
<h3 id=3D"SpringFramework6Fundamentals-SetterInjection:-"><span data-colori=
d=3D"nnivglwq0p">Setter Injection:-</span></h3>
<p><strong>Setter Injection</strong> is a type of Dependency Injection (DI)=
 where the dependencies are provided to an object via setter methods after =
the object is created. In Spring, it allows you to inject dependencies by c=
alling the setter methods of a class.</p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded=
-file-wrapper image-center-wrapper confluence-embedded-manual-size"><img cl=
ass=3D"confluence-embedded-image image-center" alt=3D"image-20240915-073718=
.png" width=3D"468" loading=3D"lazy" src=3D"2b9fc707f84c58f5b17fe87b4b4bb57=
6036b4809f3138c84a29b627bf82eb4d2" data-image-src=3D"https://thingworx.jira=
.com/wiki/download/attachments/4181721154/image-20240915-073718.png?version=
=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1726385844066&amp;cacheVersion=3D1&amp;api=3Dv2=
" data-height=3D"564" data-width=3D"1086" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"=
0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"4182016268" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1=
" data-linked-resource-type=3D"attachment" data-linked-resource-default-ali=
as=3D"image-20240915-073718.png" data-base-url=3D"https://thingworx.jira.co=
m/wiki" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D"image/png" data-linked-resourc=
e-container-id=3D"4181721154" data-linked-resource-container-version=3D"21"=
 data-media-id=3D"e2b7e7d1-f7ca-4dba-bfd1-d6ee8e56a0fd" data-media-type=3D"=
file" height=3D"242"></span>
<p>Explanation:-</p>
<p>Here are getCustomerService returns that return a bean of type customerS=
ervice or a bean named CustomerService. Notice, though, that we have a sett=
er injection here as we=E2=80=99re building our beans; we=E2=80=99re going =
to call this setCustomerRepository method on our customerService instance. =
To do that, we need to have a method getcustomerRepository in our configura=
tion that returns the customerRepository bean. This is going to wire the Cu=
stomerRepository inside of our CustomerService.</p>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro confluence-information-macro-inf=
ormation">
<span class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconfont-info confluence-informa=
tion-macro-icon"></span>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro-body">
<p>Here Spring is doing lot of magic behind scenes when a bean registered, =
such as by default beans are singletone and will execute the method the fir=
st time its called.</p>
</div>
</div>
<p></p>
<h3 id=3D"SpringFramework6Fundamentals-ConstructorInjection:-"><span data-c=
olorid=3D"xh5kfsglcl">Constructor Injection:-</span></h3>
<p></p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper image-center-wrapper=
 confluence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image i=
mage-center" alt=3D"image-20240915-081708.png" width=3D"468" loading=3D"laz=
y" src=3D"ead0fbe07ac8fcadadc8d203ce13e7e76981f14218ff604be9023185db343501"=
 data-image-src=3D"https://thingworx.jira.com/wiki/download/attachments/418=
1721154/image-20240915-081708.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D172638=
8232123&amp;cacheVersion=3D1&amp;api=3Dv2" data-height=3D"520" data-width=
=3D"884" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"418=
2311088" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"at=
tachment" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"image-20240915-081708.png" =
data-base-url=3D"https://thingworx.jira.com/wiki" data-linked-resource-cont=
ent-type=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"4181721154" dat=
a-linked-resource-container-version=3D"21" data-media-id=3D"48c161e8-fbdc-4=
29e-8e42-20dd48a8bd9d" data-media-type=3D"file" height=3D"275"></span>
<p>Difference between Constructor and Setter Injection.</p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"760" data-layout=3D"default" data-local-id=3D"99=
2a2363-c198-4cb7-af88-c1aeb5533ef9" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<tbody>
<tr>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p>Feature/Aspect</p></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p><strong>Constructor Injection</strong></p></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p><strong>Setter Injection</strong></p></th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Injection Time</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>At the time of object creation (in the constructor).</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>After object creation (via setter methods).</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Handling of Dependencies</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Mandatory dependencies must be provided.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Allows optional dependencies.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Immutability</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Promotes immutability since dependencies are set once and can't be chang=
ed.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Dependencies can be modified after creation.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Clarity of Dependencies</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Clear and visible in the constructor signature.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Not immediately visible (hidden in setters).</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Null Safety</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Ensures all required dependencies are provided, preventing <code>NullPoi=
nterExceptions</code>.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Risk of <code>NullPointerExceptions</code> if not handled properly.</p><=
/td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Flexibility</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Less flexible; dependencies are fixed once provided.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>More flexible; allows changing dependencies later.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Usage in Testing</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Easier to inject mock objects for testing since dependencies are provide=
d at creation.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Also allows injection of mocks but requires setter calls.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Parameter Overload</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Can lead to constructors with many parameters, making code harder to rea=
d.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Avoids long constructors but can result in many setter calls.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Typical Use Case</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Best for mandatory, non-changeable dependencies.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Best for optional, changeable dependencies.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Preferred Practice</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Preferred for required dependencies (especially in modern Spring apps).<=
/p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Useful for optional or late dependencies.</p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p>In summary:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Use <strong>Constructor Injection</strong> when dependencies are require=
d and should not be changed after object creation.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Use <strong>Setter Injection</strong> when dependencies are optional or =
might need to change after the object is created.</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<h3 id=3D"SpringFramework6Fundamentals-SpringScopes:-"><strong>Spring Scope=
s:-</strong></h3>
<p></p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper image-center-wrapper=
 confluence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image i=
mage-center" alt=3D"image-20240917-044242.png" width=3D"468" loading=3D"laz=
y" src=3D"1499f802cf4b62f93e056e7122d284d143534150b2f55233f536d64e502b6902"=
 data-image-src=3D"https://thingworx.jira.com/wiki/download/attachments/418=
1721154/image-20240917-044242.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D172654=
8165794&amp;cacheVersion=3D1&amp;api=3Dv2" data-height=3D"258" data-width=
=3D"1517" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"41=
85161768" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"a=
ttachment" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"image-20240917-044242.png"=
 data-base-url=3D"https://thingworx.jira.com/wiki" data-linked-resource-con=
tent-type=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"4181721154" da=
ta-linked-resource-container-version=3D"21" data-media-id=3D"6cbe4666-bdc1-=
44b9-a979-5d601763eef8" data-media-type=3D"file" height=3D"79"></span>
<p>In Spring, <strong>scopes</strong> determine the lifecycle and visibilit=
y of the beans managed by the Spring container. There are several scopes av=
ailable, each defining how Spring should handle bean instances.</p>
<h3 id=3D"SpringFramework6Fundamentals-1.SingletonScope(Default)">1. <stron=
g>Singleton Scope (Default)</strong></h3>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Description</strong>: Only one instance of the bean is created p=
er Spring IoC container, and the same instance is shared across the applica=
tion.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Usage</strong>: Default scope, typically used for stateless bean=
s like service layers.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Example</strong>:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">@Scope(=
"singleton") // or simply omit the @Scope annotation, as singleton is the d=
efault
@Component
public class MyService {
}</pre>
</div>
</div></li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"SpringFramework6Fundamentals-2.PrototypeScope">2. <strong>Prototy=
pe Scope</strong></h3>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Description</strong>: A new instance of the bean is created each=
 time it is requested from the Spring container.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Usage</strong>: For stateful beans or beans that require a new i=
nstance per operation.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Example</strong>:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">@Scope(=
"prototype")
@Component
public class MyPrototypeService {
}</pre>
</div>
</div></li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"SpringFramework6Fundamentals-3.RequestScope(WebApplicationsOnly)"=
>3. <strong>Request Scope (Web Applications Only)</strong></h3>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Description</strong>: A new instance of the bean is created for =
each HTTP request.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Usage</strong>: For beans that should only exist for the duratio=
n of a single HTTP request.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Example</strong>:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">@Scope(=
"request")
@Component
public class MyRequestScopedBean {
}</pre>
</div>
</div></li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"SpringFramework6Fundamentals-4.SessionScope(WebApplicationsOnly)"=
>4. <strong>Session Scope (Web Applications Only)</strong></h3>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Description</strong>: A new instance of the bean is created for =
each HTTP session and is shared across requests in the same session.</p></l=
i>
<li>
<p><strong>Usage</strong>: Useful for storing user session data.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Example</strong>:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">@Scope(=
"session")
@Component
public class MySessionScopedBean {
</pre>
</div>
</div></li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"SpringFramework6Fundamentals-5.GlobalSessionScope(PortletApplicat=
ions)">5. <strong>Global Session Scope (Portlet Applications)</strong></h3>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Description</strong>: A new instance of the bean is created for =
the entire global HTTP session in a portlet environment.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Usage</strong>: Specifically for portlet applications.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Example</strong>:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">@Scope(=
"globalSession")
@Component
public class MyGlobalSessionScopedBean {
}</pre>
</div>
</div></li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"SpringFramework6Fundamentals-6.CustomScopes">6. <strong>Custom Sc=
opes</strong></h3>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Description</strong>: Spring allows you to define your own custo=
m scopes if the default ones don't suit your needs.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Usage</strong>: You can create a custom scope by implementing th=
e <code>Scope</code> interface and registering it with the Spring container=
.</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"SpringFramework6Fundamentals-ChoosingaScope:">Choosing a Scope:</=
h3>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Singleton</strong> is ideal for stateless, shared beans.</p></li=
>
<li>
<p><strong>Prototype</strong> is suitable for stateful beans where each req=
uest requires a fresh instance.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Request/Session</strong> are useful in web-based applications to=
 manage request and session lifecycles.</p></li>
</ul>
<p>These scopes help manage the lifecycle of Spring beans and ensure effici=
ent resource usage based on the application=E2=80=99s needs.</p>
<p></p>
<h2 id=3D"SpringFramework6Fundamentals-Autowired:-"><code>Autowired</code>:=
-</h2>
<p>The <code>@Autowired</code> annotation in Java is a feature provided by =
the Spring Framework, primarily used for automatic dependency injection. De=
pendency injection is a design pattern that allows a class to have its requ=
ired components (dependencies) supplied externally, rather than creating th=
em internally. This promotes loose coupling and makes your code more modula=
r and testable.</p>
<h2 id=3D"SpringFramework6Fundamentals-How@AutowiredWorks">How <code>@Autow=
ired</code> Works</h2>
<p>When you use the <code>@Autowired</code> annotation on a field, construc=
tor, or setter method, Spring's dependency injection mechanism will automat=
ically inject the required bean into the class at runtime. This is done by =
scanning the application context for a matching bean type and injecting it =
where needed.</p>
<h3 id=3D"SpringFramework6Fundamentals-TypesofInjection">Types of Injection=
</h3>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><strong>Field Injection</strong>: Directly injects dependencies into fie=
lds.</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">public =
class MyService {
    @Autowired
    private DependencyService dependencyService;
}</pre>
</div>
</div></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Setter Injection</strong>: Uses setter methods to inject depende=
ncies.</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">public =
class MyService {
    private DependencyService dependencyService;

    @Autowired
    public void setDependencyService(DependencyService dependencyService) {
        this.dependencyService =3D dependencyService;
    }

    // ...
}
</pre>
</div>
</div></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Constructor Injection</strong>: Injects dependencies via the cla=
ss constructor.</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">public =
class MyService {
    private final DependencyService dependencyService;

    @Autowired
    public MyService(DependencyService dependencyService) {
        this.dependencyService =3D dependencyService;
    }

    // ...
}</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>Constructor injection is generally recommended because it allows for imm=
utable dependencies and makes your classes easier to test.</p></li>
</ol>
<h2 id=3D"SpringFramework6Fundamentals-QualifyingBeans">Qualifying Beans</h=
2>
<p>If multiple beans of the same type exist, you can use the <code>@Qualifi=
er</code> annotation alongside <code>@Autowired</code> to specify which bea=
n to inject.</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">public =
class MyService {
    @Autowired
    @Qualifier("specificDependencyService")
    private DependencyService dependencyService;

    // ...
}
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<h2 id=3D"SpringFramework6Fundamentals-OptionalDependencies">Optional Depen=
dencies</h2>
<p>To indicate that a dependency is optional, you can set the <code>require=
d</code> attribute to <code>false</code>.</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">@Autowi=
red(required =3D false)
private OptionalDependencyService optionalDependencyService;</pre>
</div>
</div>
<h2 id=3D"SpringFramework6Fundamentals-CommonPitfalls">Common Pitfalls</h2>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>No Matching Bean Found</strong>: If Spring cannot find a bean of=
 the required type, it will throw a <code>NoSuchBeanDefinitionException</co=
de>. Ensure that the bean is correctly declared and scanned.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Multiple Matching Beans</strong>: If multiple beans of the same =
type are found and no qualifier is specified, Spring will throw a <code>NoU=
niqueBeanDefinitionException</code>.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Circular Dependencies</strong>: Be cautious of circular dependen=
cies, where two or more beans are dependent on each other, as this can caus=
e runtime errors.</p></li>
</ul>
<h2 id=3D"SpringFramework6Fundamentals-BestPractices">Best Practices</h2>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Use Constructor Injection</strong>: This makes your components e=
asier to test and promotes immutability.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Avoid Field Injection</strong>: While convenient, field injectio=
n can make testing more difficult and hides dependencies.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Specify Qualifiers When Necessary</strong>: Use <code>@Qualifier=
</code> to resolve ambiguity when multiple beans of the same type are prese=
nt.</p></li>
</ul>
<h2 id=3D"SpringFramework6Fundamentals-Conclusion">Conclusion</h2>
<p>The <code>@Autowired</code> annotation is a powerful tool in the Spring =
Framework that simplifies dependency management in your application. By und=
erstanding how to use it effectively, you can write cleaner, more maintaina=
ble code.</p>
<p><strong>References</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://spring.io/projects/spring-fra=
mework" rel=3D"nofollow">Spring Framework Documentation</a></p></li>
<li>
<p><a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://docs.spring.io/spring-framewo=
rk/docs/current/reference/html/core.html#beans-dependencies" rel=3D"nofollo=
w">Spring Dependency Injection Guide</a></p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<h2 id=3D"SpringFramework6Fundamentals-1.SpringComponentScanningOverview"><=
strong>1. Spring Component Scanning Overview</strong></h2>
<p><strong>Component Scanning</strong> is a mechanism in Spring that automa=
tically detects and registers beans (i.e., components) within the applicati=
on context based on specified criteria. Instead of manually declaring each =
bean, Spring scans specified packages to find classes annotated with specif=
ic stereotypes and registers them as beans.</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">+------=
----------------+          +---------------------------+
|                      |          |                           |
|   Package Structure  |          |       Spring Context      |
|                      |          |                           |
| +------------------+ |          | +-----------------------+ |
| | @Component       | |  Scan    | | Bean Registry         | |
| | @Service         | | -------&gt; | | - ComponentBean       | |
| | @Repository      | |          | | - ServiceBean         | |
| | @Controller      | |          | | - RepositoryBean      | |
| +------------------+ |          | +-----------------------+ |
|                      |          |                           |
+----------------------+          +---------------------------+
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Explanation:</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><strong>Package Structure:</strong> Contains classes annotated with Spri=
ng stereotypes like <code>@Component</code>, <code>@Service</code>, <code>@=
Repository</code>, and <code>@Controller</code>.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Scan:</strong> Spring's component scanning mechanism scans the s=
pecified packages.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Spring Context:</strong> Detected classes are registered as bean=
s within the Spring Application Context's Bean Registry.</p></li>
</ol>
<p></p>
<h2 id=3D"SpringFramework6Fundamentals-2.StereotypeAnnotationsinSpring"><st=
rong>2. Stereotype Annotations in Spring</strong></h2>
<p>Spring provides several <strong>stereotype annotations</strong> that ser=
ve as specializations of <code>@Component</code>. These annotations help in=
 categorizing beans and can carry additional semantics, which can be levera=
ged for specific functionalities.</p>
<h3 id=3D"SpringFramework6Fundamentals-a.@Component"><strong>a. </strong><c=
ode>@Component</code></h3>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Generic stereotype for any Spring-managed comp=
onent.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Usage:</strong> When a class doesn't fit into more specific cate=
gories.</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Example:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">import =
org.springframework.stereotype.Component;

@Component
public class GenericComponent {
    // Business logic
}
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<h3 id=3D"SpringFramework6Fundamentals-b.@Service"><strong>b. </strong><cod=
e>@Service</code></h3>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Indicates that an annotated class holds busine=
ss logic.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Usage:</strong> Typically used in the service layer.</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Example:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">import =
org.springframework.stereotype.Service;

@Service
public class UserService {
    // Business logic related to users
}
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<h3 id=3D"SpringFramework6Fundamentals-c.@Repository"><strong>c. </strong><=
code>@Repository</code></h3>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Indicates that an annotated class is a Data Ac=
cess Object (DAO).</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Usage:</strong> Facilitates exception translation into Spring's =
<code>DataAccessException</code> hierarchy.</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Example:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">import =
org.springframework.stereotype.Repository;

@Repository
public class UserRepository {
    // Data access logic
}
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<h3 id=3D"SpringFramework6Fundamentals-d.@Controller"><strong>d. </strong><=
code>@Controller</code></h3>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Indicates that an annotated class serves as a =
web controller.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Usage:</strong> Typically used in the presentation layer (e.g., =
handling HTTP requests).</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Example:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">d. @Con=
troller
Purpose: Indicates that an annotated class serves as a web controller.
Usage: Typically used in the presentation layer (e.g., handling HTTP reques=
ts).
Example:</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p></p>
<p>Diagram: Stereotype Annotations Hierarchy</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">       =
    +----------------+
           |   @Component   |
           +----------------+
                  ^
                  |
    +-------------+-------------+-------------+
    |             |             |             |
+---------+  +----------+  +------------+  +-------------+
| @Service|  | @Repository| | @Controller| | Other Stereotypes|
+---------+  +----------+  +------------+  +-------------+
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>Explanation:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>All stereotype annotations (<code>@Service</code>, <code>@Repository</co=
de>, <code>@Controller</code>) are specializations of <code>@Component</cod=
e>.</p></li>
<li>
<p>This hierarchy allows component scanning to detect any of these annotati=
ons as components.</p></li>
</ul>
<h2 id=3D"SpringFramework6Fundamentals-3.HowComponentScanningWorks"><strong=
>3. How Component Scanning Works</strong></h2>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><strong>Configuration:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>XML-Based Configuration</strong>:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">&lt;con=
text:component-scan base-package=3D"com.example.app"/&gt;</pre>
</div>
</div></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Java-Based Configuration:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">import =
org.springframework.context.annotation.ComponentScan;
import org.springframework.context.annotation.Configuration;

@Configuration
@ComponentScan(basePackages =3D "com.example.app")
public class AppConfig {
    // Additional bean configurations if necessary
}
</pre>
</div>
</div></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Scanning Process:</strong><br>
Spring scans the specified base packages and sub-packages.<br>
It identifies classes annotated with <code>@Component</code> or its special=
izations.<br>
Each detected class is registered as a bean in the Application Context.</p>=
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Bean Registration:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Beans can be singleton or have other scopes based on their annotations o=
r configurations.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Dependencies are injected based on annotations like <code>@Autowired</co=
de>, <code>@Inject</code>, or constructor injection.</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ol>
<h3 id=3D"SpringFramework6Fundamentals-Diagram:ComponentScanningFlow"><stro=
ng>Diagram: Component Scanning Flow</strong></h3>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">+------=
-----------------+
|   Application Config  |
|  (Java/XML Config)    |
+----------+------------+
           |
           v
+-----------------------+
|  Component Scanner    |
| (Scans base packages) |
+----------+------------+
           |
           v
+-----------------------+       +----------------------+
|  Detected Annotations | ----&gt; |  Bean Definitions    |
| @Component, @Service, |       | (Registered in IoC   |
| @Repository, @Controller|     |  Container)          |
+-----------------------+       +----------------------+
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p></p>
<h2 id=3D"SpringFramework6Fundamentals-5.PracticalExamplewithDiagrams"><str=
ong>5. Practical Example with Diagrams</strong></h2>
<p><strong>Let's walk through a simple Spring application structure to illu=
strate component scanning and stereotype annotations.</strong></p>
<h3 id=3D"SpringFramework6Fundamentals-a.ProjectStructure"><strong>a. Proje=
ct Structure</strong></h3>
